{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause proven, fix committed (not yet pushed)\n\n**Commit:** `206125736d` on `fix/12e4-fetch-abort` (worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/fix/12e4-fetch-abort`).\n\n### Proven root cause\n\n`_fetch_origin` built its git argv with no `http.lowSpeedLimit` / `http.lowSpeedTime`, so git's curl handle had no throughput-keyed abort and a connection that was established but moved zero bytes was bounded only by the wall-clock `subprocess.run(timeout=_GIT_TIMEOUT)` at 300s.\n\n### Discriminating experiment (local listener, no paid calls)\n\n| scenario | config | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| stall, 0 B/s | none (before) | still running at the 45s harness cap |\n| stall, 0 B/s | limit=1000, time=5 | aborts **5.1s**, `Operation too slow` |\n| stall, 0 B/s | limit=1000, time=2 | aborts **2.1s** |\n| dribble 2000 B/s, 60s | limit=1000, time=5 | **not aborted** |\n| dribble 4000 B/s, 20s | limit=1000, time=2 | **not aborted** (fails later as `transfer closed`) |\n\nReal-remote safety: 5 warm fetches (0.4-0.6s) and **3 cold full clones of the 80 MB mirror at 87.8 / 88.4 / 101.4s** all complete under limit=1000 / time=10. A legitimately slow 90-second transfer is not aborted.\n\n### Replication through the real entry point\n\n`resolve_ref` against a wedged remote: **30.2s** (3 attempts x 10s) vs the 300s ceiling.\n\n### Mutation evidence (both directions)\n\n- Drop the low-speed args (re-seed the exact root cause) -> stall test + argv test RED.\n- Force attempts to 1 -> retry test RED.\n- Raise the floor 100000x so the abort is effectively wall-time-keyed -> **the slow-but-progressing test goes RED**. This is the one that matters: it proves the discriminator would catch the failure mode that is worse than the bug.\n- Refactoring litmus: renamed 4 internals (`argv`, `attempts`, `floor`, `window`) -> all 4 still pass. Not change-detector tests.\n\n### Forced module split\n\n`repo_snapshot.py` was 788/800 LOC, so the fix could not land without splitting. The git-subprocess + fetch-locking cluster moved whole into `_snapshot/git_fetch.py` along the seam it already formed. 788 -> 610; new module 326. Dependency is one-directional.\n\n### Sibling sweep\n\nThree other 300s network fetches share the exposure and are filed as 851e-19ef-31dd-4e38 (`discovered_from` this ticket): `review_bot/gerrit_client.py:367`, `opcert_service/workspace.py:107,124`, `_commands/init.py:398,419`. Left out of this change deliberately.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0. Full suite re-running on the clean tree.\n\nNOT pushed to Gerrit; ticket left open per instruction."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785726354398458001,"uuid":"b498efe9-7210-4fc4-992f-effef90660e7"}